    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Change\n\n`POST /api/owners` now records a `bulkSignupWarning` flag: `true` when **more than 80** owners had already been created for the owner's registration day before this one, else `false`. It's exposed on the owner response (including subsequent `GET`s, which the acceptance test asserts).\n\nI followed the existing `namesakeCount` precedent exactly \u2014 a snapshot computed at creation time, persisted, and mapped to the DTO.\n\n## Files touched\n\n1. **`FlagBulkSignup.java`** (new function step) \u2014 mirrors `CountNamesakes`: counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals this owner's (already business-day-adjusted by `BuildOwner`, matching `RejectOverDailyLimit`'s accumulation) and sets `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(count > 80)`. Runs before save, so `findAll()` sees only pre-existing owners (\"already created\").\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `flagBulkSignup` between `countNamesakes` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `bulk_signup_warning` `Boolean` column with getter/setter.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n5. **Schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column.\n\n6. **`hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a trailing `NULL` to the positional owner seed inserts (h2/postgres use named-column inserts, so they were unaffected).\n\nThe threshold constant lives in `FlagBulkSignup.BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD = 80`, and the comparison `> 80` gives the warning a true window of 81\u2013100 (the daily hard limit at 100 still rejects via the existing rule).",
